# Copy to .env. This is the one place for values that must survive a restart but must never
# enter the repository, which is public. .env is gitignored, kept at mode 600, and named in
# deploy/checks.sh as a file that must never be tracked.
#
# Every command reads it — the API, the scheduler, the backup job, the notifier — anchored to
# the data directory rather than to whatever directory you happened to run from
# (agentic_trading/env.py, and the same parsing in deploy/macos/common.sh for the shell
# scripts). A value already in the environment always wins over a line here.
#
# Prefer this over `launchctl setenv`: that does not survive a reboot, and nothing announces
# the loss. Macro data quietly returns to "unavailable" and the off-site backup quietly stops.
#
# After editing, restart the service so running processes pick it up:
#   deploy/macos/release.sh publish        (or: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.local.agentic-trading.api)

# ── data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DO NOT set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY anywhere. The LLM layer runs on your Claude Max
# subscription through the Claude Code CLI; an API key would switch billing to
# pay-as-you-go. The adapter also strips these variables before every call.
#
# Free, one minute to get, at https://fred.stlouisfed.org (My Account → API Keys).
# Without it every run records CPI, core PCE, unemployment, the fed funds rate and the 10-year
# yield as missing evidence, lowers its confidence and prefers NO_TRADE.
FRED_API_KEY=
# Only if you change data_vendors in config/investor_profile.yaml.
ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=

# ── off-site backup ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A directory on other hardware or in a synced folder. The mirror is AES-256 encrypted before
# it leaves this machine. The directory must already exist: the backup refuses to create it,
# so an unplugged disk fails loudly instead of writing an "off-site" copy to the boot disk.
CT_BACKUP_MIRROR=
# A file holding the passphrase for that encrypted mirror.
CT_BACKUP_KEY_FILE=

# ── notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed for the webhook / WeCom / WeChat channels. The webpush channel signs with a key
# pair generated on this machine (state/vapid_key.json) and needs none of these -- but it does
# need CT_PUSH_SUBJECT below.
CT_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK=
CT_NOTIFY_TOKEN=
CT_WECOM_WEBHOOK=
CT_WECHAT_WEBHOOK=
# The contact this deployment gives Apple's push service, as an https address or a mailbox you
# read. Apple validates it and answers anything it dislikes with 403 BadJwtToken -- which looks
# exactly like a broken key -- so web push reaches no device until this is set. It names the
# machine, which is why it lives here and not in the tracked, public config.
CT_PUSH_SUBJECT=
# Where the console lives, as an https address (the tailnet name this Mac serves it on). Messages
# link to the right screen with it; unset, they still say what happened. Kept here rather than in
# config/risk_profile.yaml because it names the machine.
CT_CONSOLE_URL=

# An external watcher that expects a regular ping. Nothing on this Mac can report that this Mac
# is gone, so silence here is the only signal an outage produces.
CT_HEARTBEAT_URL=
